# Phase 5: ImageKit Integration & Vision AI Clustering

Let's integrate media hosting capabilities so your knowledge base can intelligently store, cluster, and "understand" images and videos.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. New Utilities & Dependencies
- **[NEW Dependency]** `imagekit` to handle backend uploads.
- **[NEW] `src/utils/imagekit.js`**: A centralized service configuring the ImageKit SDK and exposing a reliable upload function.

### 2. Backend Modifications

#### [MODIFY] `src/controllers/item.controller.js`
- When a `file` is uploaded, explicitly check its mimetype buffer (`image/png`, `video/mp4`, etc.). 
- If media, instantly upload it strictly via `ImageKit` before background processing begins.
- Save the resulting ImageKit URL as the item's `url`, and set its fundamental `type` to "media".

#### [MODIFY] `src/workers/itemworker.js` & `src/utils/tagger.js`
- Enhance the AI tagger to utilize **Gemini's Vision AI capabilities**. If an image is presented, we forward the actual image data to Gemini to visually interpret and describe the image, extracting semantic tags and a comprehensive title (e.g., "A diagram outlining Kubernetes container orchestration").
- This textual description will then be heavily vectorized and placed firmly into Qdrant for graph and cluster matching!

#### [MODIFY] `src/controllers/cluster.controller.js`
- Expand the explicit deterministic routing architecture:
   - Any document with a media-type of Image intrinsically maps to an **"Images"** folder in the Clusters dashboard.
   - Any document with a media-type of Video inherently maps to a **"Videos"** folder.

